# UST.G3BT H02 Endpoint Action at One Split Prime

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_ONE_SPLIT_PRIME_OPERATOR_ACTION`

## Theorem

Let `gamma` satisfy the selected irreducible sextic used by the G3BI correction
direction, and reduce at `p = 21817`, where that sextic has the six distinct
roots

```text
5, 1971, 6912, 10062, 10605, 14055.
```

At every root, evaluate the exact selected G3BI H02 endpoint chart and the
complete family of `1,013` characteristic-zero G3BK source columns
`R_P = -4 P s C`. Then:

1. every `42,706 x 42,706` endpoint chart is invertible;
2. every complete `42,706 x 1,013` inverse action has zero residual;
3. the six sparse actions determine the unique full action in
   `F_21817[gamma]/(m_gamma)` through the displayed Lagrange transform; and
4. the complete `248 x 1,013 x 6` quotient power-basis tensor is emitted and
   re-evaluates at all six roots with zero mismatches.

The six endpoint determinants are

```text
419, 13232, 2913, 6224, 10294, 7871  (mod 21817).
```

The full action is retained without loss as six exact sparse evaluation
matrices plus the invertible Lagrange transform. This is an exact finite-ring
representation, not a numerical approximation.

## Scope

This theorem closes the one-split-prime H02 source-active action. It does not
reconstruct the action over `Q(gamma)`: that promotion still requires
independent split primes and a proved height bound, or an independent exact
annihilating relation. It also does not prove recursive return of the H02
preimages, integral path transport, or the terminal physical readout.

